	quests: [
		{
			dependencies: ["210200000000000E"]
			description: [
				"&f&lThermal Series.&r"
				""
				"Mekanism, EnderIO and Industrial Foregoing all solve the same problem: power goes in, processed resources come out. They also all ask you to learn a whole system before the first machine turns over."
				""
				"&eThermal&r and &eImmersive Engineering&r are the two gentlest ways into that problem, and they approach it from opposite ends."
				""
				"Thermal is the softest landing in the pack - one block, one job, drop in a fuel, done. Immersive Engineering is the opposite: nothing is a single block, everything is a structure you build out of parts and walk inside."
			]
			icon: "thermal:machine_pulverizer"
			id: "7E20000000000001"
			rewards: [
				{
					count: 8
					id: "7E20000000000101"
					item: "minecraft:iron_ingot"
					type: "item"
				}
				{
					id: "7E20000000000102"
					type: "xp"
					xp: 50
				}
			]
			shape: "hexagon"
			size: 1.5d
			subtitle: "&7Two more ways to process a rock"
			tasks: [{
				id: "7E20000000000201"
				title: "Pick a second industry"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			title: "&bThe Second Industry"
			x: -10.0d
			y: 0.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7E20000000000001"]
			description: [
				"Thermal's machines all run on Forge Energy, so you need a little first."
				""
				"The &eStirling Dynamo&r burns solid fuel - coal, charcoal, anything from the sieve chain - and pushes FE straight into an adjacent machine. No cables needed for your first setup: put the dynamo flush against the machine and it feeds it directly."
				""
				"&7Every Thermal dynamo takes augments too, so this same block scales up later rather than being replaced."
			]
			icon: "thermal:dynamo_stirling"
			id: "7E20000000000002"
			rewards: [{
				id: "7E20000000000103"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 30
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Burn something, get power"
			tasks: [{
				id: "7E20000000000202"
				item: "thermal:dynamo_stirling"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&bThe Stirling Dynamo"
			x: -8.0d
			y: -3.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7E20000000000002"]
			description: [
				"The &ePulverizer&r is the reason most people install Thermal: it grinds one ore into &etwo dust&r, and often a bonus product on the side."
				""
				"On a skyblock where every ore came out of a sieve, doubling is enormous."
				""
				"Note the GUI - one input, one output, a power bar, and an augment tray. That is the entire Thermal interface, and every machine after this one looks the same."
			]
			icon: "thermal:machine_pulverizer"
			id: "7E20000000000003"
			rewards: [{
				id: "7E20000000000104"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 40
			}]
			shape: "gear"
			subtitle: "&7One ore in, two dust out"
			tasks: [{
				id: "7E20000000000203"
				item: "thermal:machine_pulverizer"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&bThe Pulverizer"
			x: -6.0d
			y: -3.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7E20000000000003"]
			description: [
				"The &eInduction Smelter&r takes two inputs and fuses them - ore plus sand for extra yield, or two dusts into an alloy."
				""
				"It is Thermal's answer to Mekanism's infuser and EnderIO's alloy smelter, and it will happily process the ores and dusts those mods produce. Nothing here is walled off; the pack's ore chains all speak to each other."
			]
			icon: "thermal:machine_smelter"
			id: "7E20000000000004"
			rewards: [{
				id: "7E20000000000105"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 40
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Two in, one better thing out"
			tasks: [{
				id: "7E20000000000204"
				item: "thermal:machine_smelter"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&bThe Induction Smelter"
			x: -4.0d
			y: -3.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7E20000000000004"]
			description: [
				"The &eCentrifugal Separator&r pulls mixed inputs apart into their components - the cleanup step at the end of a processing line."
				""
				"Feed it slag, dusts, mob drops or the odd by-products the rest of your machines spit out, and it sorts them into something usable instead of something you throw away."
			]
			icon: "thermal:machine_centrifuge"
			id: "7E20000000000005"
			rewards: [{
				id: "7E20000000000106"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 40
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Turn by-products back into products"
			tasks: [{
				id: "7E20000000000205"
				item: "thermal:machine_centrifuge"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&bThe Centrifugal Separator"
			x: -2.0d
			y: -3.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7E20000000000002"]
			description: [
				"Thermal's &eDucts&r carry energy and fluids. They are cheap, they auto-connect, and they hide inside walls neatly."
				""
				"&c&lWorth knowing:&r this version of Thermal Dynamics has &lno item duct&r - only &eEnergy&r and &eFluid&r ducts. Moving items is left to Pipez, Pretty Pipes, XNet or SFM, all of which are already in this pack. Don't go hunting for a duct that isn't there."
			]
			icon: "thermal:energy_duct"
			id: "7E20000000000006"
			rewards: [{
				id: "7E20000000000107"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 30
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Energy and fluids only"
