			y: -1.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7E20000000000005"]
			description: [
				"The &ePhytogenic Insolator&r grows crops with power instead of time - drop in a seed and some water and it returns a full harvest plus extra seeds."
				""
				"It stacks neatly with the &eMystical Agriculture&r essence farm you already run and with &eBotany Pots&r: pots for hands-off passive growth, the Insolator for when you want a specific crop &oright now&r and have power to spend."
			]
			icon: "thermal:machine_insolator"
			id: "7E20000000000008"
			rewards: [{
				id: "7E2000000000010A"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 50
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Crops, but with a power bill"
			tasks: [{
				id: "7E20000000000208"
				item: "thermal:machine_insolator"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&bThe Phytogenic Insolator"
			x: -2.0d
			y: -1.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7E20000000000001"]
			description: [
				"Thermal's generators are called &eDynamos&r, and there are five: Stirling (solid fuel), Compression (liquid fuel), Magmatic (lava), Numismatic (coins and gems) and Lapidary (gems)."
				""
				"&e&lThey all take the same augments&r, which is the point of Thermal - one upgrade system across every machine and dynamo."
				""
				"&7Fuel Catalysts make fuel last longer; Boost augments raise output at the cost of efficiency. Pick per dynamo depending on whether fuel or throughput is your constraint.&r"
				""
				"&8The Magmatic Dynamo pairs with your Cyclic Melter loop - infinite cobble to lava to power."
			]
			icon: "thermal:dynamo_stirling"
			id: "14FFE2FBE2F681B0"
			rewards: [{
				id: "494BDBAF9AB38444"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 30
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Thermal's generators"
			tasks: [{
				id: "217A15E140B6EE9B"
				item: "thermal:dynamo_stirling"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&bDynamos"
			x: -8.0d
			y: 3.0d
		}
		{
			description: [
				"&eAugments&r slot into every Thermal machine and dynamo, and they are what makes the mod worth using."
				""
				"&e&lThe main families:&r"
				"&7- &fUpgrade&7 - raises the machine's whole tier at once"
				"&7- &fSpeed / Efficiency&7 - the usual trade"
				"&7- &fAuxiliary&7 - machine-specific extras like extra output chance"
				"&7- &fFluid / Item tank&7 - bigger internal buffers"
				""
				"&c&lAugment slots are limited by machine tier&r, so an Upgrade augment often pays for itself by unlocking more slots."
				""
				"&7Because it is one system, anything you learn on a Pulverizer applies to every other Thermal block you ever place.&r"
			]
			icon: "thermal:machine_crafter"
			id: "23EBEFE4863B832A"
			rewards: [{
				id: "6A6C2102A8D1E39D"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 30
			}]
			subtitle: "&7One upgrade system, every machine"
			tasks: [{
				id: "1039DBA3E52DBC2C"
				item: "thermal:machine_crafter"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&bAugments"
			x: -8.0d
			y: 4.5d
		}
		{
			description: [
				"The &ePulverizer&r grinds ore into dust; the &eRedstone Furnace&r smelts it. Together they are Thermal's 2x ore chain."
				""
				"&e&lThey are the cheapest ore doubling in the pack&r and available very early - well before Mekanism's chain is practical."
				""
				"&7Both have auto-eject, so chaining them with no pipes at all works: pulverizer facing furnace facing a chest.&r"
				""
				"&8The Pulverizer also gives bonus outputs - nickel from iron, gold from copper - which Mekanism's chain does not."
			]
			icon: "thermal:machine_pulverizer"
			id: "4112F538CDB724AE"
			rewards: [{
				id: "644248EE08257724"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 30
			}]
			subtitle: "&7The starter pair"
			tasks: [
				{
					id: "32992EEF4FFFFCCF"
					item: "thermal:machine_pulverizer"
					type: "item"
				}
				{
					id: "79B6C072D0CBC064"
					item: "thermal:machine_furnace"
					type: "item"
				}
			]
			title: "&bPulverizer & Redstone Furnace"
			x: -6.0d
			y: 3.0d
		}
		{
			description: [
				"The &eInduction Smelter&r combines two inputs - the alloying machine, and Thermal's route to richer ore processing."
				""
				"&e&lWith Rich Slag or Cinnabar it produces extra output&r, taking Thermal's ore chain past simple doubling."
				""
				"&7It makes every Thermal alloy: Electrum, Invar, Constantan, Signalum, Lumium, Enderium. Those alloys are what the higher machines and augments are built from.&r"
			]
			icon: "thermal:machine_smelter"
			id: "106E634AC77EF6C0"
			rewards: [{
				id: "7C8CCF6C8EB27400"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 30
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Alloys and 3x ore"
			tasks: [{
				id: "741D82B9BA02E526"
				item: "thermal:machine_smelter"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&bInduction Smelter"
			x: -6.0d
			y: 4.5d
		}
		{
			description: [
				"The &eCentrifugal Separator&r splits materials into components; the &eMagma Crucible&r melts solids into fluids; the &eBlast Chiller&r freezes fluids into solids."
				""
				"&e&lThe Crucible is the useful one here&r - it turns cobblestone into lava directly, which feeds Magmatic Dynamos and your obsidian line without a Cyclic Melter."
				""
				"&7The Centrifuge processes mob drops, ores and sludge into usable components. It is the tidiest way to deal with Industrial Foregoing's by-products.&r"
			]
			icon: "thermal:machine_centrifuge"
			id: "005F815DB6D33895"
			rewards: [{
				id: "161D8C95BED459CC"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 30
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Centrifuge, Crucible, Chiller"
			tasks: [
				{
					id: "48CA954D6F3EBD3E"
					item: "thermal:machine_centrifuge"
					type: "item"
				}
				{
					id: "3326926563DEF4C2"
					item: "thermal:machine_crucible"
					type: "item"
				}
			]
			title: "&bFluid Machines"
			x: -4.0d
			y: 3.0d
		}
		{
			description: [
				"Thermal's &eDevices&r are cheap single-purpose blocks: Collector, Nullifier, Item Buffer, Fluid Buffer, XP Collector, Rock Gen, Water Gen, Tree Extractor."
				""
				"&e&lThe Rock Gen and Water Gen are quietly excellent on a skyblock&r - infinite stone and infinite water with no build, no lava, no pool."
				""
				"&7The Nullifier is a void bin. The Collector is a vacuum. The Buffers are filtered inline storage with throughput control.&r"
				""
				"&8None of them are exciting. Most of them remove a chore you have been tolerating."
			]
			icon: "thermal:machine_insolator"
			id: "40A26ECD0EA04DE4"
			rewards: [{
				id: "37E2C14EA92038F5"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 30
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Small blocks, large effect"
			tasks: [{
				id: "3821322E574EB59F"
				item: "thermal:machine_insolator"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&bDevices"
			x: -4.0d
			y: 4.5d
		}
		{
			description: [
				"Thermal's &eDucts&r carry energy, fluid and items, and they are among the cheapest transport in the pack."
				""
				"&e&lItemducts have built-in filtering and round-robin&r without needing a separate sorter block, which makes small sorting jobs very quick to build."
				""
				"&7They connect straight to any FE machine, so a Thermal duct network can carry Mekanism, AE2 and Create power equally well.&r"
			]
			icon: "thermal:energy_duct"
			id: "76133BE8A70ABAC1"
			rewards: [{
				id: "2D8E2CF6BE77AC74"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 30
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Thermal's transport"
			tasks: [{
				id: "562710CFDA54D604"
				item: "thermal:energy_duct"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&bFluiducts & Itemducts"
			x: -2.0d
			y: 3.0d
		}
		{
			description: [
				"Every Thermal machine can have its sides configured for input, output or nothing, and its internal tanks and slots locked."
				""
				"&e&lAuto-eject is the setting that matters.&r Turn it on and the machine pushes output to whatever is adjacent - which is why a Thermal setup often needs no pipes at all."
				""
				"&7Redstone control on every machine lets you gate production on a signal without extra blocks.&r"
			]
			icon: "thermal:machine_press"
			id: "35F24D7A725C1F44"
			rewards: [{
				id: "03F95A7CB31D9109"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 30
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Every machine, every side"
			tasks: [{
				id: "111B8CF8099AA3EC"
				item: "thermal:machine_press"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&bTinkering & Reconfiguration"
			x: -2.0d
			y: 4.5d
		}
		{
			description: [
				"&6&lThermal is the least glamorous mod in this pack and one of the most useful.&r"
				""
				"One augment system across every block. Auto-eject that removes pipes entirely. Ore doubling available before anything else offers it. And a Rock Gen that quietly solves the skyblock's oldest problem."
				""
				"&7Nothing here is required. Most of it makes everything else easier.&r"
			]
			icon: "thermal:machine_smelter"
			id: "7F0D7093E391B6E5"
			min_required_dependencies: 1
			rewards: [{
				id: "45C19325C69C8712"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 30
			}]
			subtitle: "&7The quiet workhorse"
			tasks: [{
				id: "6151036D82890666"
				title: "Complete"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			title: "&b&lThermal Complete"
			x: 0.0d
			y: 3.8d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7E20000000000001"]
			description: [
				"&aThermal Cultivation&r adds the farming half of the Thermal series."
				""
				"&e&lThe useful part is &fPhytosoil&r&e:&r soil that grows crops without water and takes fertiliser for a straight yield increase."
				""
				"&7The Watering Can works by hand or in a dispenser. Phyto-Gro is the fertiliser, made in the Insolator from any plant matter.&r"
				""
				"&8On a void island this pairs well with Botany Pots - Phytosoil for volume, pots for automation."
			]
			icon: "thermal:phytosoil"
			id: "2693C2D41FA82007"
			rewards: [{
				id: "4D74A782967C6CD0"
